# House rule 6 is about code, and this file is where "code" is drawn.
#
# The formatter owns what it can reformat without changing what a sentence
# says: TypeScript, the JavaScript configs, JSON. Everything below is prose or
# is governed elsewhere, and running a code formatter over it would reflow
# paragraphs that were written a line at a time to be read a line at a time.
#
#   *.md        doc-lint.sh owns markdown well-formedness, and this tree's
#               prose is hand-wrapped. A reflow would produce a diff on every
#               file, touching every line, for no reader's benefit.
#   .chug/      shell, and check-shell-quoting.sh is what judges it.
#   model/      Quint, which Prettier does not parse.
#   .claude/    not this tree's file to format.
#
# A file this list covers is not unformatted; it is formatted by whatever gate
# names it above. What has no such gate is TypeScript, which is exactly what is
# left in scope.

node_modules/
*.md
.chug/
.githooks/
model/
.claude/
package-lock.json
